<article class="env-lemma" id="06NF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06NF">Lemma <span data-tag="06NF">66.4.10</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $U$ be a scheme and let $f : U \to X$ be an étale morphism. Let $X' \subset X$ be the open subspace corresponding to the open $|f|(|U|) \subset |X|$ via Lemma <a href="/tag/03BZ" data-tag="03BZ">66.4.8</a>. Then $f$ factors through a surjective étale morphism $f' : U \to X'$. Moreover, if $R = U \times _ X U$, then $R = U \times _{X'} U$ and $X'$ has the presentation $X' = U/R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The existence of the factorization follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/03IE" data-tag="03IE">66.4.9</a>. The morphism $f'$ is surjective according to Lemma <a href="/tag/03H5" data-tag="03H5">66.4.4</a>. To see $f'$ is étale, suppose that $T \to X'$ is a morphism where $T$ is a scheme. Then $T \times _ X U = T \times _{X'} U$ as $X' \to X$ is a monomorphism of sheaves. Thus the projection $T \times _{X'} U \to T$ is étale as we assumed $f$ étale. We have $U \times _ X U = U \times _{X'} U$ as $X' \to X$ is a monomorphism. Then $X' = U/R$ follows from Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0262" data-tag="0262">65.9.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>